// shader-differential — all-channel vertex program (NOT under test).
//
// Successor to sd_pos_uv.vcg for the auto-binder (increment 3): every
// interpolated channel a fragment program under judgment may read is
// driven by a deterministic function of the quad's (u,v), so both
// sides of a pair see identical inputs and any reader gets defined
// data instead of stale registers.  TEXCOORD0.xy is (u, v) as it was in
// sd_pos_uv.vcg, so texture coordinates are what every earlier row saw;
// its z and w now vary like every other lane (2026-09-02 constants
// audit), so a row reading them sees a changed input - by design.
//
// Channel recipe (u,v in 0..1 across the RT, v down):
//   TEXCOORD0 = (u, v, 0.1 + 0.5v, 0.7 + 0.25u)   texture coordinates (xy); z, w vary
//   TEXCOORD1 = (u - 0.5, v - 0.5, 0.3 + 0.4u, 0.4 + 0.5v)   a "normal"-shaped vector
//   TEXCOORD2 = (0.5 - u, 0.35 + 0.3v, v, 0.25 + 0.5u)   a "half"/"eye"-shaped vector
//   TEXCOORD3 = (u * v, u + v, 1 - u, 0.6 + 0.3u)   mixed products
//   COLOR0    = (u, v, 1 - u, 0.5 + 0.5 v)   per-vertex colour with alpha ramp
// Nothing is normalised here: shaders that normalise do so themselves,
// shaders that dot raw vectors get finite, varying values.
//
// NO LANE IS A CONSTANT: a constant lane is an identity for some
// operation (w == 1 for a lerp or a projective divide, z == 0 for a dot
// product term), and an identity hides a dropped or wrong use of that
// lane - the default path's dropped fog lerp on th06_notex was invisible
// while TEXCOORD2.w was 1 (t_72810bd7, 2026-09-01).  A shader reading any
// lane sees a value that varies across the image.  Measured at the 64x64
// pixel centres (2026-09-02): no lane is exactly 0 or 1 at any pixel
// except TEXCOORD3.y = u + v, which is exactly 1 on the anti-diagonal
// (64 of 4096 pixels; its range is 0.016..1.98), and TEXCOORD1.xy /
// TEXCOORD2.x change sign across the centre lines without hitting 0 at a
// pixel centre.  Two lanes may coincide on isolated curves (continuous
// functions of (u, v) do) - at most 65 of 4225 sample points for the
// closest pair (claude, review of e53d763).  An identity or a coincidence
// confined to a line is not blindness: a row judges 4096 pixels and the
// other 98% still show a dropped or swapped lane.

void main(
    float2 in_position       : POSITION,
    float2 in_texcoord       : TEXCOORD0,
    out float4 out_position  : POSITION,
    out float4 out_texcoord0 : TEXCOORD0,
    out float4 out_texcoord1 : TEXCOORD1,
    out float4 out_texcoord2 : TEXCOORD2,
    out float4 out_texcoord3 : TEXCOORD3,
    out float4 out_color     : COLOR0)
{
    float u = in_texcoord.x;
    float v = in_texcoord.y;
    out_position  = float4(in_position.x, in_position.y, 0.0f, 1.0f);
    out_texcoord0 = float4(u, v, 0.1f + 0.5f * v, 0.7f + 0.25f * u);
    out_texcoord1 = float4(u - 0.5f, v - 0.5f, 0.3f + 0.4f * u, 0.4f + 0.5f * v);
    // .w varies: a fragment shader that uses a texcoord's w as a lerp or
    // scale factor collapses to identity at w == 1, and every channel used
    // to carry 1 there - the default path's dropped fog lerp on th06_notex
    // (lerp by fog.w) was pixel-invisible for that reason (2026-09-01 23:22).
    out_texcoord2 = float4(0.5f - u, 0.35f + 0.3f * v, v, 0.25f + 0.5f * u);
    out_texcoord3 = float4(u * v, u + v, 1.0f - u, 0.6f + 0.3f * u);
    out_color     = float4(u, v, 1.0f - u, 0.5f + 0.5f * v);
}
